{"name":"Virtual Golf","hex":"#c1ee13","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"virtual","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["In effect or essence, rather than in fact or reality; also, imitated, simulated.","For practical purposes, though not technically; almost complete, very near."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Preceded by the: that which is imitated or simulated rather than existing in fact or reality;  an instance of this.\n That which is simulated in a computer and/or online; virtual reality;  an instance of this; specifically , a computer simulation of a real-world sport such as horse racing.","That which is simulated in a computer and/or online; virtual reality;  an instance of this; specifically , a computer simulation of a real-world sport such as horse racing."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/virtual"},{"term":"golf","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of Golf of the ICAO/NATO radiotelephony alphabet."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A ball game played by individuals competing against one another in which the object is to hit a ball into each of a series of (usually 18 or nine) holes in the minimum number of strokes.","Alternative letter-case form of Golf from the NATO/ICAO Phonetic Alphabet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/golf"}],"entries":[{"title":"List of Sega Saturn games","blocks":[{"text":"The Sega Saturn is a 32-bit fifth-generation home video game console that was developed by Sega and first released on November 22, 1994. Its games are in CD-ROM format, and its game library contains several arcade ports as well as original titles. There are 1028 games on this list not including non-game software and compilations of Saturn games. 775 of those games were released as Japan-only exclusives, which makes up 75% of the list. For games that were announced or in development for the Saturn, but never released, see the list of cancelled Sega Saturn games."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/Sega-Saturn-JP-Mk1-Console-Set.png/330px-Sega-Saturn-JP-Mk1-Console-Set.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_Sega_Saturn_games"},{"title":"Golf simulator","blocks":[{"text":"A golf simulator is an indoor electronic simulator that allows to hit a physical golf ball into a projection screen. The system uses the measured data to calculate the ball's flight and display it on the screen. Depending on the system, measurements may include clubhead speed, ball speed, launch angle, spin rate, club path, and carry distance. The data is used to calculate the relationships to the ball's flight performance, by adding environmental aspects, including terrain, wind, rain and other such influences or obstacles. Modern golf simulators are used for golf practice, instruction, club fitting, and entertainment."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/New_Sports_Simulator_%286917965%29.jpg/330px-New_Sports_Simulator_%286917965%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Golf_simulator"},{"title":"Golf","blocks":[{"text":"Golf is a club-and-ball sport in which players use various clubs to hit a ball into a series of holes on a course in as few strokes as possible. The game was first played in the 15th century in Scotland, and as such, the country is often accredited as \"the home of Golf\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/Golfer_swing.jpg/330px-Golfer_swing.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Golf"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Sega-Saturn-Console-Set-Mk1.png/500px-Sega-Saturn-Console-Set-Mk1.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Sega-Saturn-Console-Set-Mk1.png/1280px-Sega-Saturn-Console-Set-Mk1.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Sega-Saturn-Console-Set-Mk1.png/500px-Sega-Saturn-Console-Set-Mk1.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASega-Saturn-Console-Set-Mk1.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Rep._Vestal_on_indoor_golf_course_in_House_gym_LCCN2016841856.jpg/500px-Rep._Vestal_on_indoor_golf_course_in_House_gym_LCCN2016841856.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Rep._Vestal_on_indoor_golf_course_in_House_gym_LCCN2016841856.jpg/1280px-Rep._Vestal_on_indoor_golf_course_in_House_gym_LCCN2016841856.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Rep._Vestal_on_indoor_golf_course_in_House_gym_LCCN2016841856.jpg/500px-Rep._Vestal_on_indoor_golf_course_in_House_gym_LCCN2016841856.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Albert Henry Vestal in an indoor golf driving range. (1926)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARep._Vestal_on_indoor_golf_course_in_House_gym_LCCN2016841856.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/GOLFZON_2.jpg/330px-GOLFZON_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/GOLFZON_2.jpg/330px-GOLFZON_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Projector-based golf simulator","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGOLFZON_2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c